      {
        "id": 230573,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-05-12T22:37:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Exclusivity has been fixed to mean that one exclusive bonus&nbsp;<em>and</em>&nbsp;one exclusive penalty can be used on a single roll.&nbsp; However, the rules still erroneously say that a mod affects one die and not one effect.</p>\n<p>There is&nbsp;<em>no</em>&nbsp;change to how bonuses and penalties cancel each other out.&nbsp; That's important because Christopher did it a different way (and taught everyone else his way) in SCRPG Live Season 3.&nbsp; His way was wrong.</p>\n<p>Accident's Reflexive&nbsp;Burst now triggers on zone change, not just the first time you're attacked at close range per scene.&nbsp; Much more versatile, though it could whiff if you change zones with no close enemies.</p>\n<p>Training&nbsp;<em>gained</em>&nbsp;access to Intellectual Powers, actually.&nbsp; But always Be Prepared got nerfed from Max to Mid&nbsp;die.</p>\n<p>Genius's Overwhelming Vision is also now completely different (and pretty good!).</p>\n<p>Gadgeteer's Snap Decision now boosts only yourself.</p>\n<p>Modular's Destroyer's ability's change isn't just superficial or a clarification, like most of the other \"changes.\" It now modifies basic Attacks specifically.&nbsp; This has implications for various interactions, e.g. Inspiring Totem.</p>\n<p>Critical Eye (Red Information) is clarified.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:05:36.195Z",
